<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
    =============================================================================
    HealthMap — App Privacy Manifest
    Required by Apple since May 1, 2024 for every iOS app submitted to the App
    Store that uses UserDefaults or any "required reason API". Missing or
    incomplete manifests trigger automatic rejection during submission.

    Read this before changing anything:
      - NSPrivacyTracking is FALSE — HealthMap never links first-party data with
        third-party data "for the purpose of tracking" (ATT glossary). No IDFA,
        no cross-app/site user correlation, no ad networks. All analytics is
        first-party (PostHog EU project dedicated to HealthMap, Supabase
        analytics_events table owned by us).
      - Every "Linked" collected data type has NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking
        set to FALSE for the same reason. Product Interaction linkage exists
        solely for product analytics keyed by Supabase user_id; it never leaves
        our infrastructure.
      - Required-reason APIs declared: UserDefaults (CA92.1) and file
        timestamps (C617.1, `MealThumbnailStore.purgeOld`). If you add new
        system API usage (ATTrackingManager, disk space, system boot time,
        active keyboards), declare them here AND in Sentry's own manifest if
        they're reached via Sentry. The widget extension has its OWN manifest
        (`KiwioWidgets/PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy`).
    =============================================================================
    -->

    <key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
    <false/>

    <!-- No tracking domains because NSPrivacyTracking is false. -->
    <key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
    <array/>

    <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
    <array>

        <!-- ==== Email address ==== -->
        <!-- Collected at sign-up/sign-in, linked to the Supabase user_id for
             authentication and password reset. Never used for advertising. -->
        <dict>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
            <string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeEmailAddress</string>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
            <true/>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
            <false/>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
            <array>
                <string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
            </array>
        </dict>

        <!-- ==== Name ==== -->
        <!-- First name captured during sign-up or via Sign in with Apple on
             the very first sign-in (Apple drops it afterwards — see
             `DatabaseService.bootstrapAppleProfile`). Used to personalize the
             dashboard greeting and recommendations. -->
        <dict>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
            <string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeName</string>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
            <true/>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
            <false/>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
            <array>
                <string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
                <string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeProductPersonalization</string>
            </array>
        </dict>

        <!-- ==== Health ==== -->
        <!-- Questionnaire responses (diet, symptoms, medications, goals) and
             the AI deficiency analysis derived from them. These are RGPD
             Article 9 "special category" data — collected with explicit
             consent during the onboarding questionnaire, stored in the
             Supabase `profiles.questionnaire_data` JSONB column, and erased
             on account deletion (`DatabaseService.deleteAllUserData`). -->
        <dict>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
            <string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeHealth</string>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
            <true/>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
            <false/>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
            <array>
                <string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
                <string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeProductPersonalization</string>
            </array>
        </dict>

        <!-- ==== Fitness ==== -->
        <!-- Apple Santé, lecture seule (`HealthKitService`) : le nombre de pas
             du jour devient le niveau d'activité du profil, envoyé avec le
             questionnaire (`profiles.questionnaire_data`). L'énergie active
             brûlée ne sert qu'à la jauge du Journal, sur l'appareil. Le poids
             et le sommeil importés relèvent de Health (ci-dessus). -->
        <dict>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
            <string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeFitness</string>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
            <true/>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
            <false/>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
            <array>
                <string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
                <string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeProductPersonalization</string>
            </array>
        </dict>

        <!-- ==== Photos or Videos ==== -->
        <!-- Photos de repas (caméra ou `PhotosPicker`) et photo d'une prise de
             sang : envoyées à notre serveur pour l'analyse IA, puis jetées —
             aucune photo n'est gardée côté serveur (aucun bucket de stockage
             utilisateur), seules les valeurs lues le sont. Déclarées parce que
             les octets transitent par notre infrastructure et par l'IA.
             La dictée d'un repas (`VoiceMealService`) n'est PAS de l'audio
             collecté : SFSpeechRecognizer transcrit sur l'appareil quand il le
             peut, sinon chez Apple ; seul le TEXTE atteint `parse-meal-voice`,
             qui n'est pas gardé non plus — seul le repas du Journal l'est
             (Health). D'où aucune déclaration AudioData. -->
        <dict>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
            <string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePhotosorVideos</string>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
            <true/>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
            <false/>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
            <array>
                <string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
            </array>
        </dict>

        <!-- ==== Purchase History ==== -->
        <!-- Abonnements Premium : RevenueCat (StoreKit 2) et notre table
             `receipt_transactions` (vérification du reçu par `verify-receipt`)
             gardent la formule, les dates et l'identifiant de transaction,
             rattachés au compte. Aucun moyen de paiement : Apple seul le
             connaît. -->
        <dict>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
            <string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurchaseHistory</string>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
            <true/>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
            <false/>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
            <array>
                <string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
            </array>
        </dict>

        <!-- ==== User ID ==== -->
        <!-- L'identifiant Supabase Auth du compte : clé de toutes les lignes en
             base, `appUserID` RevenueCat (`SubscriptionService.identify`),
             `user_id` des statistiques d'usage (`analytics_events`). -->
        <dict>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
            <string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeUserID</string>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
            <true/>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
            <false/>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
            <array>
                <string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
                <string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAnalytics</string>
            </array>
        </dict>

        <!-- ==== Product Interaction ==== -->
        <!-- Tab taps, screen views, questionnaire progress, checkin events.
             Sent to PostHog EU and to Supabase `analytics_events` with the
             `user_id` column populated. Never leaves our infrastructure.
             The forbidden-keys allow-list in `AnalyticsService.sanitize`
             guarantees no PII or health content is embedded in payloads. -->
        <dict>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
            <string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeProductInteraction</string>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
            <true/>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
            <false/>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
            <array>
                <string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAnalytics</string>
                <string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
            </array>
        </dict>

        <!-- ==== Crash Data ==== -->
        <!-- Captured by Sentry. Linked to the Supabase user_id because
             `CrashReportingService.identify(userId:)` is called after
             sign-in. `sendDefaultPii` is disabled and `beforeSend` strips
             email / questionnaire_data / ai_analysis — see the service
             for the full allowlist. -->
        <dict>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
            <string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeCrashData</string>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
            <true/>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
            <false/>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
            <array>
                <string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
            </array>
        </dict>

        <!-- ==== Performance Data ==== -->
        <!-- Sentry auto-performance traces (enableAutoPerformanceTracing=true
             with a 10% prod sample rate). Linked to user_id for the same
             reason as Crash Data. -->
        <dict>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
            <string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePerformanceData</string>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
            <true/>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
            <false/>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
            <array>
                <string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAnalytics</string>
            </array>
        </dict>

    </array>

    <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
    <array>
        <!-- ==== UserDefaults (CA92.1) ==== -->
        <!-- Usage sites (33 occurrences across 6 files as of audit):
               - ContentView: @AppStorage("hasSeenOnboarding")
               - AuthViewModel: clearLocalCaches() wipes "healthmap_*" keys
                 on sign out (mirrors the web app's localStorage cleanup)
               - GamificationService: streak, best streak, total checkins,
                 earned badges, zen mode toggle
               - ScoreHistoryService: local cache of the last N score rows
                 for offline chart rendering
               - ScoreHistoryView: @AppStorage for range selection
               - CheckinViewModel: last-checkin-date throttling

             Ces UserDefaults ne sont lus que par l'app elle-même (CA92.1).
             Les widgets ne les voient pas : l'app leur parle par un TROUSSEAU
             partagé (`keychain-access-groups` fr.healthmap.app.partage,
             `Partage/BoiteCommune.swift`), pas par un App Group. L'extension
             a son propre manifeste pour son repli UserDefaults local.
             No Shared Web Credentials. -->
        <dict>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
            <string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
            <array>
                <string>CA92.1</string>
            </array>
        </dict>

        <!-- ==== File timestamps (C617.1) ==== -->
        <!-- `MealThumbnailStore.purgeOld` lit la date de modification
             (`contentModificationDateKey`) des vignettes de repas rangées
             dans le conteneur de l'app, pour jeter celles de plus de 30
             jours. Fichiers du conteneur de l'app uniquement : C617.1. -->
        <dict>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
            <string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp</string>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
            <array>
                <string>C617.1</string>
            </array>
        </dict>
    </array>
</dict>
</plist>
